    "title": "Heck embraces player-coach role",
    "text": "Grafton junior cross country runner Kyza Heck has been busy making up for lost time. A budding distance runner since her grade-school days in Bottineau’s BIO Girls club, Heck picked up cross country as a seventh grader but ran into trouble a few years later. She suffered a stress-fractured ankle at Grafton’s season-opening meet two years ago, and kept running [[…]](https://www.wcrecord.com/articles/heck-embraces-player-coach-role/)\nYou must be a digital subscriber to access this content. Please login below or subscribe today!",
